Sval: what WebDriver opens never shares the user's cookie jar

A window WebDriver opens gets a workspace of its own, named WebDriver and
isolated, and its first tab opens in that workspace's jar, or in a user
context the client made over BiDi if it names one.
WindowManager.openBrowserWindow, which classic NewWindow and BiDi's
browsingContext.create both reach, asks SvalWebDriver to open it. A tab a
client opens in one of the user's windows goes to a window of WebDriver's
instead (SvalWebDriver.tabTarget, from TabManager.addTab and from BiDi's
browsingContext.create, whose wait for the old tab to hide must watch that
window), and is the first tab of a window opened for it when there is none.
browser.createUserContext reports each context it makes to SvalWebDriver,
and those are the only jars besides its window's own that TabManager.addTab
passes on: any other, the default one included, which BiDi names for every
tab a client opens without naming one, gives way to the window's workspace
jar (workspace-jar-for-new-tabs.patch). No chrome API reaches inside the
remote agent, and the jar has to be chosen before the window or tab exists:
Sval reopening a tab in another jar would end the client's browsing context.

